From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000072 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: read stub latch uncached

The stub-page-latch physical log reaches marker 0x51510015, but records a
zero latch value. The latch is written through CKSEG1 when the copied stub is
installed, while the late assembly gate reads it through KSEG0. On the physical
device that cached read can see stale data even though QEMU observes the write.

Read and clear the latch through KSEG1 as well. Keep the branch target itself
in KSEG0 so the copied stub still executes from the cached identity text path.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/entry.S | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
@@ -163,7 +163,7 @@
 	li	k0, 0x1002
 	bne	k1, k0, 1f
 	 nop
-	li	k0, 0x80401068
+	li	k0, 0xa0401068
 	lw	k1, 0(k0)
 	lui	k0, 0xa13f
 	sw	k1, 24(k0)
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@
 	bne	k1, k0, 1f
 	 nop
 	li	k1, 0
-	li	k0, 0x80401068
+	li	k0, 0xa0401068
 	sw	k1, 0(k0)
 	lui	k0, 0xa13f
 	li	k1, 0x51510007
-- 
2.45.0
